1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.059
With my hands, I craft code.

2
00:00:03.059 --> 00:00:14.314
I weave words, magic at my fingertips, creating
worlds, one line at a time, in a terminal or in poetry.

3
00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:19.340
Sometimes it compiles, sometimes it's a haiku.

4
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.399
I'm a cultivator of stories.

5
00:00:22.399 --> 00:00:24.257
Hi, I'm Rheana M.

6
00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:31.577
Mindo, a soon-to-be BS Computer Science student graduate from UPLB.

7
00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:46.000
I'd like to think of myself as someone who likes to build things,
systems, stories, and sometimes spaghetti code that works anyways.

8
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.250
I believe tech should be useful, thoughtful, and fun, just like this video.

9
00:00:53.250 --> 00:01:01.167
From Philippine Science High School to UPLB,
I've followed my curiosity in the world of coding.

10
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:08.000
I'm graduating with honors thanks to
great mentors, hot choco, and Stack Overflow.

11
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.720
My thesis?

12
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:26.791
I'm studying how AI might be biased towards certain religions, and I'm developing an equalizing loss function to help
make these models fairer to all faiths while maintaining their performance, a topic that is close and dear to my heart.

13
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:39.899
Thanks to the DOST-SEI and UP SLAS scholarships, I was able to trade in my decade-old
laptop for a powerful new one, fueling my passion for tech and making my dreams more achievable.

14
00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:52.000
I've been lucky to compete in Informatics Olympiads, rank in national contests, and
represent the Philippines across Asia, sharpening my skills one algorithm at a time.

15
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.527
From ICPC to city apps, bridges to bug hunts, I've
stumbled, learned, and leveled up with every line of code.

16
00:02:00.527 --> 00:02:07.490
It's been a journey of grit, growth, and just
the right amount of anime to keep me going.

17
00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:20.633
At UPLB Computer Science Society, I've led initiatives that made computer science
more accessible, from CompSci 101 articles to mock exams that reach over 400 students.

18
00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:30.020
I also worked with developers in building a real-time Code
Wars platform for a flagship competitive programming contest.

19
00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:37.374
As Kaiban's treasurer, I handled 10 fundraising
events, reformed financial systems, gained 64.

20
00:02:37.374 --> 00:02:45.119
7% profit, and increased our budget by 756%, all
while keeping events affordable at just 100 pesos.

21
00:02:45.119 --> 00:02:56.071
At Azeus, I helped develop an AI-powered RAG chatbot using LangChain,
integrating Redmine data to optimize search and information retrieval.

22
00:02:56.071 --> 00:03:11.248
I've managed teams of up to 20 developers, built platforms for room reservation, developed
COVID-19 contact tracing mobile app, other software, and even created Arduino bots back in high school.

23
00:03:11.248 --> 00:03:16.333
My stack includes Python, React, SQL, Firebase, and all of these.

24
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:23.765
But I've learned that leadership, collaboration,
and clear documentation are just as essential.

25
00:03:23.765 --> 00:03:32.449
And while I don't run on caffeine, I do rely on
teamwork, motivational music, and a well-named variable or two.

26
00:03:32.449 --> 00:03:33.075
My goal?

27
00:03:33.075 --> 00:03:40.741
To join a company where I can ship tech that
matters, tools that don't just function but resonate.

28
00:03:40.741 --> 00:03:47.000
Whether it's writing a script or writing
backend logic, I bring the same energy.

29
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:57.364
I thrive in fast-paced interdisciplinary teams where
I can wear many hats and occasionally a party hat.

30
00:03:57.364 --> 00:03:59.545
What makes me different?

31
00:03:59.545 --> 00:04:02.273
I'm a dev with a poet's heart.

32
00:04:02.273 --> 00:04:07.727
I code, I write, I lead, I listen, I even play the recorder.

33
00:04:07.727 --> 00:04:17.818
If you need a teammate who adapts fast, delivers well,
and brings a healthy dose of nerdy jokes, I'm your girl.

34
00:04:17.818 --> 00:04:20.909
I'm not just a software developer.

35
00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:25.364
I'm a builder, a storyteller, a lifelong learner.

36
00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:33.273
I'm versatile, driven, fun, and ready to
create something magical with code and beyond.

37
00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.091
That's what makes me different.

38
